# Docker build context for the MCP sidecar image.
#
# node_modules must be excluded for two reasons. The Dockerfile installs
# dependencies itself (COPY package.json + npm install), so shipping a host copy
# would be redundant and could carry platform-specific binaries built for the wrong
# architecture. More importantly, CDK hashes this directory to decide whether the
# image asset changed — so a stray local `npm install` here (for instance to run the
# server on a workstation) would change the hash and force a full image rebuild and
# ECR push on the next deploy, which also means the deploy suddenly requires Docker.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Never part of an image.
.env
.env.*
*.log
